  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "The number of new flu cases is decreasing at a rate of 5% per week. How long will it take for the number of new flu cases to reach a quarter of its current level? Answer to the nearest whole number of weeks.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "27 weeks.",
      "worked": "Let $N_0$ be the current number of new cases and $t$ the time in weeks. The weekly decay factor is $1-0.05=0.95$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N(t)&=N_0(0.95)^t\\\\N_0(0.95)^t&=\\frac{N_0}{4}\\\\(0.95)^t&=\\frac14\\\\\\log_{10}(0.95)^t&=\\log_{10}\\frac14\\\\t\\log_{10}0.95&=\\log_{10}\\frac14\\\\t&=\\frac{\\log_{10}(1/4)}{\\log_{10}0.95}\\\\t&\\approx27.0268\\end{align*}$$\n\nIt will take approximately 27 weeks, to the nearest whole week.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
